{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My strength and my song is Yah.</b> He called it 'my strength' in the manner of what is written (Psalms 68): ״צוה אלהיך עזך״; and 'my song is Yah' — וזמרתי ליה, from the language of (II Samuel 23): ״ונעים זמירות ישראל״, and it is written (Psalms 47): ״זמרו אלהים זמרו״. <br><b>And He has become my salvation.</b> The redemption from Egypt is called ישועה because after it there was exile; but the future redemption, after which there is no exile, is called ישועות, as is said (Psalms 53): ״מי יתן מציון ישועות ישראל״, and likewise it is called תשועת עולמים, as is said (Isaiah 45): ״ישראל נושע בה' תשועת עולמים״. And so too this song is called שירה in the feminine because there is destined to come after it another exile, just as the female conceives and gives birth and returns and conceives again; but for the future we find שיר in the masculine, as it is written (Psalms 98): ״שירו לה' שיר חדש כי נפלאות עשה״ and so on, and it is written (Isaiah 26): ״ביום ההוא יושר השיר הזה״ and so on." "<b>This is my El and I will glorify Him.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): ואנוהו — I will build Him a dwelling (נוה); and therefore He mentioned (Exodus 15:13) ״נוה קדשך״, and the Temple is called נוה, as is said (Jeremiah 31): ״יברכך ה' נוה צדק הר הקדש״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: ״זה אלי ואנוהו״ — I will beautify His honored name in the eyes of all the nations, so that they will say: There is none like HaShem our Elohim. And so Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Song of Songs 5): ״מה דודך מדוד היפה בנשים״ — for thus you are put to death for the sanctification of His name, as is said (Song of Songs 1): ״על כן עלמות אהבוך״ — על מות אהבוך, even when they are put to death they do not deny Your name, as is said (Psalms 44): ״כי עליך הורגנו כל היום״. Rabbi Eliezer says: From where do you say that a maidservant saw at the sea what Ezekiel son of Buzi did not see? As is said: ״זה אלי ואנוהו״. In Ezekiel it is written (Ezekiel 1): ״ואראה מראות אלהים״, and in the case of the other prophets it is written (Hosea 12): ״וביד הנביאים אדמה״ — that is, through likenesses and visions; but at the sea they all saw, until each and every one said: ״זה אלי ואנוהו״. And the intent of the Sages in this is not that the maidservant's attainment in understanding and wisdom surpassed the attainment of Ezekiel son of Buzi the prophet; rather, the intent is that a maidservant saw at the sea a thing that Ezekiel did not see. Another interpretation: ואנוהו — I will beautify myself before Him with mitzvot: a beautiful tallit, a beautiful sukkah, a beautiful lulav. <b>The Elohim of my father and I will exalt Him.</b> I will make mention of His exaltation."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "The citation מה דודך מדוד היפה בנשים is labeled (Song of Songs 5) but the verse appears in Song of Songs 5:9; the pun על כן עלמות / על מות is on Song of Songs 1:3, labeled (Song of Songs 1); both rendered exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:26.567319117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}